### Key semantics
- `exceptionPayloads`: class MODULE → payload-enum module. **Class identity is
  the meaning**; two exception classes in one module collide (last-scanned-wins)
  — this is the xs-crossmod defect.
- `payloadEnumNames`/`payloadEnumOwners`: payload-enum MODULE → enum name /
  owner class. Collide only if two payload ENUMS share one module (other axis).
- `payloadEnumModules`: enum MODULE → emitted module path. Emission location is
  genuinely a module property; module keying is correct here.

